  "critique": {
    "axis": "aesthetics",
    "evidence": "Strong cyber-lab art direction, restrained cyan/amber accents, and clear metric hierarchy across viewports. However, desktop composition leaves excessive dead space around the hero, while mobile becomes dense and visually tiring: tiny mono labels, long technical strings, tight card padding, and stacked borders weaken legibility. Tablet/mobile headers also look abruptly clipped rather than elegantly responsive, with faint navigation text and uncertain contrast evidence.",
    "fix": "Refine responsive spacing and type: reduce desktop hero dead space, raise mobile mono/body sizes and contrast, wrap or abbreviate hashes, add breathing room between evidence rows, and give the scrollable header a clearer fade/active-state treatment so clipping feels intentional.",
